  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Congoville (2021), published by Leuven University Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 1,613 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Congoville by Pieter Boons and Sandrine Colard was published by Leuven University Press in 2021. Conceptually, the work connects to Exhibition, Mythology, Colonialism, The Imaginary and Utopia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 1,613 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 1 library collection. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
